@startuml Scenario_3_Topics_and_Disciplines

title Topics and Disciplines Within a Channel\nWhy disciplines are topics, not channels

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam rectangle {
    RoundCorner 10
}

rectangle "**iTwin: Bridge 9340 Corridor**\nFederation ID: aaa-111-..." as itwin #E3F2FD {

    rectangle "**Single Channel**\n/mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication" as chan #FFF3E0 {
        rectangle "Topic: bentley:imodel/structural/changeset" as t1 #FFECB3
        rectangle "Topic: bentley:imodel/mechanical/changeset" as t2 #FFECB3
        rectangle "Topic: bentley:imodel/civil/changeset" as t3 #FFECB3
        rectangle "Topic: oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry" as t4 #C8E6C9
    }
}

actor "Structural\nEngineer" as SE
actor "Mechanical\nEngineer" as ME
actor "AssetWise\nALIM" as ALIM
actor "Analytics\nDashboard" as DASH

SE --> t1 : publishes
ME --> t2 : publishes

t1 --> ALIM : subscribes to\nstructural only
t4 --> ALIM : subscribes to\nProcessRegistry
t1 --> DASH : subscribes to\nall topics
t2 --> DASH
t3 --> DASH
t4 --> DASH

note bottom of chan
  **One channel, multiple topics**
  Each subscriber picks the topics it needs.
  Cross-discipline subscriber: one subscription, all topics.
  Single-discipline subscriber: one subscription, one topic.

  **Alternative rejected: channel per discipline**
  Would create 4× channels (24 total for 6 domains)
  Cross-discipline subscriber needs 4 subscriptions
  Same security, same owner, same lifecycle — no reason to split
end note

@enduml
